{
  "info": {
    "name": "02 - Persistencia PostgreSQL - Backend (tests)",
    "description": "Casos de prueba para la API del Módulo 02 (FastAPI + psycopg + PostgreSQL). Backend en http://localhost:8000\n\nFlujo Feliz: 8 requests que cubren el CRUD completo + la PERSISTENCIA.\nCasos limite: 6 requests que validan errores 422 y 404.\n\nDIFERENCIA CLAVE vs Módulo 01: los datos viven en PostgreSQL.\nEl request \"PERSISTENCIA\" es el corazon de la clase: reinicia el\nservidor y la tarea sigue ahi.\n\nPara correr todo de una: Collection Runner (boton Run).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Flujo Feliz",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Health check (verifica BBDD)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "http://localhost:8000/api/health",
            "description": "En el Módulo 01 el health contaba los elementos de una lista en memoria. Ahora ejecuta SELECT COUNT(*) contra PostgreSQL: si la BBDD no responde, este endpoint falla. Es la prueba de que la API habla con la base de verdad."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"BBDD conectada\", () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body.status).to.eql(\"Funciona\");",
                  "  pm.expect(body.db).to.eql(\"conectada\");",
                  "  pm.expect(typeof body.tasks_count).to.eql(\"number\");",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Listar tareas (inicial)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "http://localhost:8000/api/tasks",
            "description": "GET /api/tasks. Con la tabla vacia devuelve [] (array vacio). Fijate que la respuesta es IDENTICA a la del Módulo 01: mismo JSON, mismos campos. El contrato de la API no cambio."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"Devuelve un array\", () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(Array.isArray(body)).to.be.true;",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "3. Crear tarea valida",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"title\": \"Aprender SQL con PostgreSQL\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "http://localhost:8000/api/tasks",
            "description": "POST /api/tasks. Fijate lo que NO enviamos: ni id, ni completed, ni created_at. La base los genera sola con sus DEFAULT. El id que devuelve se guarda en la variable {{task_id}} para los tests siguientes."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status 201\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test(\"Estructura de tarea\", () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property(\"id\");",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property(\"title\");",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property(\"completed\");",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property(\"created_at\");",
                  "  pm.expect(body.completed).to.be.false;",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test(\"Guardar id en variable\", () => {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set(\"task_id\", pm.response.json().id);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "4. Listar con datos",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "http://localhost:8000/api/tasks",
            "description": "GET /api/tasks. Ahora la lista tiene la tarea creada en el paso 3. Los datos vienen de PostgreSQL, no de una lista de Python."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"Hay al menos 1 tarea\", () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body.length).to.be.at.least(1);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "5. Toggle completada",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [],
            "url": "http://localhost:8000/api/tasks/{{task_id}}",
            "description": "PATCH /api/tasks/{id}. El UPDATE lo hace PostgreSQL con \"SET completed = NOT completed\". El toggle que en el Módulo 01 hacia Python ahora lo hace la base, en una sola operacion atomica."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"Quedo completada\", () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().completed).to.be.true;",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "6. Toggle de vuelta (estado se guarda)",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [],
            "url": "http://localhost:8000/api/tasks/{{task_id}}",
            "description": "PATCH de nuevo: completed vuelve a false. En el Módulo 01 esto dependia del estado en memoria; aca el estado vive en la fila de la tabla. Cada toggle es un UPDATE real en PostgreSQL."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"Volvio a no completada\", () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().completed).to.be.false;",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "7. PERSISTENCIA - reinicia el servidor",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "http://localhost:8000/api/tasks",
            "description": "EL MOMENTO DE LA CLASE:\n1. Anda a la terminal donde corre el backend y mata el servidor (Ctrl+C)\n2. Volve a ejecutar: uv run main.py\n3. Ejecuta este request\n\nLa tarea creada en el paso 3 DEBE seguir ahi. En el Módulo 01, reiniciar el servidor significaba perder todo. Hoy los datos viven en PostgreSQL: sobreviven al reinicio del backend, a los apagones, a todo.\n\nEso es PERSISTENCIA."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"Los datos SOBREVIVIERON\", () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body.length).to.be.at.least(1);",
                  "  pm.expect(body.some(t => t.title === \"Aprender SQL con PostgreSQL\")).to.be.true;",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "8. Eliminar tarea",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [],
            "url": "http://localhost:8000/api/tasks/{{task_id}}",
            "description": "DELETE /api/tasks/{id}. Devuelve { \"ok\": true } si la fila existia y se borro."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"Respuesta ok\", () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().ok).to.be.true;",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Casos limite",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Titulo vacio -> 422",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"title\": \"\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "http://localhost:8000/api/tasks",
            "description": "Pydantic valida que title no este vacio (min_length=1). Mismo error 422 que el Módulo 01: el contrato de validacion tampoco cambio."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status 422\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(422));",
                  "pm.test(\"Error string_too_short\", () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body.detail[0].type).to.eql(\"string_too_short\");",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Titulo de 201 caracteres -> 422",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"title\": \"AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "http://localhost:8000/api/tasks",
            "description": "Pydantic valida el limite superior (max_length=200). Mismo 422 string_too_long del Módulo 01."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status 422\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(422));",
                  "pm.test(\"Error string_too_long\", () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body.detail[0].type).to.eql(\"string_too_long\");",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "3. Sin body -> 422",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": ""
            },
            "url": "http://localhost:8000/api/tasks",
            "description": "POST sin body: falta el campo title. Pydantic responde 422 missing."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status 422\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(422));",
                  "pm.test(\"Error missing\", () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body.detail[0].type).to.eql(\"missing\");",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "4. PATCH tarea inexistente -> 404",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [],
            "url": "http://localhost:8000/api/tasks/999999",
            "description": "PATCH de un id que no existe: UPDATE no toca ninguna fila, fetchone() devuelve None y FastAPI responde 404 con el mismo mensaje del Módulo 01."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status 404\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(404));",
                  "pm.test(\"Detail no encontrada\", () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body.detail).to.include(\"no encontrada\");",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "5. DELETE tarea inexistente -> 404",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [],
            "url": "http://localhost:8000/api/tasks/999999",
            "description": "DELETE de un id que no existe: RETURNING no devuelve filas -> 404."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status 404\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(404));",
                  "pm.test(\"Detail no encontrada\", () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body.detail).to.include(\"no encontrada\");",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "6. Title no string -> 422",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"title\": 123\n}"
            },
            "url": "http://localhost:8000/api/tasks",
            "description": "POST con title numerico: Pydantic no lo acepta como string y responde 422 string_type. La API valida los tipos antes de tocar la base."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status 422\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(422));",
                  "pm.test(\"Error string_type\", () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body.detail[0].type).to.eql(\"string_type\");",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
